The Provider shall deliver the following {{term: services}} to each Client:

- Platform hosting, monitoring, and capacity management
- Application development against an agreed backlog
- Technical support during {{term: business-hours}}
- Monthly performance reporting, delivered within {{duration: 5, unit=D}} of month end

## Environments {#service-environments}

The Provider shall maintain a production environment and at least one non-production environment
for each Client. The reference topology is shown below.

![Reference platform topology](diagrams/topology.png)

Each {{term: deliverable}} is promoted to production only after the commissioning Client has
accepted it in the non-production environment. {#service-promotion}

### Promotion Procedure {#service-promotion-procedure}

Promotion follows these steps in order:

1. The Provider deploys the {{term: deliverable}} to the non-production environment
2. The Client tests it and records acceptance or defects within {{duration: 10, unit=D}}
3. On acceptance, the Provider schedules the production release
4. The Provider confirms completion and updates the release log

#### Rollback {#service-rollback}

If a production release fails acceptance testing, the Provider shall roll back to the previous
release within {{duration: 4, unit=H}} and report the cause to the Client.

The Provider publishes its current platform status at
[status.acme.example](https://status.acme.example).

## Service Availability {#service-availability}

The Provider shall maintain production availability of 99.9% measured monthly, excluding scheduled
maintenance notified at least {{duration: 7, unit=D}} in advance.

Availability is measured by an automated health check issued every {{duration: 30, unit=S}} from
at least two independent monitoring locations.

Scheduled maintenance shall be performed outside {{term: business-hours}} wherever practicable.
